              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Can standard cron run tasks every 30 seconds?</h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
                Standard POSIX/Unix crontab does not support seconds; its minimum resolution is one minute (<code class="text-white font-mono">1m</code>). However, frameworks like Quartz (Java), Spring, and Node-cron support 6-field cron expressions with a seconds column. For Unix crontab, running twice a minute is achieved by running two commands with a <code class="text-white font-mono">sleep 30</code> offset.
              </p>
